@name Explainer 4: cemented achromat 50mm f/8
# Explainer #4: cemented achromat (N-BK7 crown + F2 flint), stop at the
# lens, f/8: a telescope-objective (Fraunhofer) doublet.
# Role: two glasses cancel axial colour and spherical aberration; sharp
# centre, bad corners (astigmatism, field curvature).
# Design: three curvatures vary (EFL 50 mm), minimising the white-light RMS
# spot on axis plus the Seidel coma, object at 2.5 m.
# Rows match 05-landscape (stop first) so the video can morph them.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/04-achromat.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/8, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 1.0 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
  stop        0.5000      air            3.127
  31.0932     4.0000      N-BK7          7.050
  -17.4879    2.0000      F2             7.050
  -64.7690    46.0000     air            7.050
